in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/spectral/consent
in @mirror/spectral/morphism
in @epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth

# @mirror/fracture/keyword — the kintsugi fracture body that resolves a
# `prism @X/Y` sub-prism declaration to `glass @X/Y` per the
# keyword/depth discipline.
#
# THE OPERATIONAL HALF of recognition #46's bilateral pattern. The
# declarative half landed at
# `@epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth` (sibling tick); this
# shard names the auto-fracture the kintsugi loop applies when the
# property's transparency surfaces a keyword/depth opacity. Per Alex's
# verbatim recognition: "The kintsugi formatter can have an auto
# `fracture` that resolves sub-prisms to `glass`." The substrate names
# the resolver here; the kintsugi driver composes it through
# `@mirror/spectral/oscillate`'s `active_pass`.
#
# Load-bearing context: recognition #46 (keyword_matches_depth
# property; pending); recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert
# space; promoted) — fracture bodies are how the substrate maintains
# coherence by resolving keyword-level distinctions at each Bateson
# level. The `/` separator deepens the level; the keyword must track
# the level; this fracture body restores the tracking when it drifts.
#
# === The bilateral pattern (candidate recognition #53) ===
#
# `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` declares WHAT must hold; a
# matching `@mirror/fracture/<predicate>` declares HOW to restore the
# property when it fails. The pair is bilateral in the same shape as
# the cybernetic/algedonic finding from the cybernetic-foundation
# work's §4: a sensing surface (the property's transparency report) +
# an acting surface (the fracture body's mutation) form one complete
# loop at the kintsugi altitude.
#
# Candidate recognition #53 (property/fracture bilateral pattern):
# flagged for promotion review; not unilaterally promoted by this
# tick. The substrate now carries one concrete instance of the
# pattern (this shard + the sibling property); the second instance
# (the forward-promised `@mirror/fracture/predicate` against
# `@epistemologic/property/<topology-predicate>` per the materialize
# training set's #21 prophecy) is the witness that would lift the
# pattern from candidate to recognised.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# The materialize training set (per `shards/code/rust/materialize.mirror`
# §"The 30th-instance training set, lifted") forward-promises
# `@mirror/fracture/predicate` as the home for fracture proposals
# derived from topology. The `@mirror/fracture` family root is named
# but not yet declared at depth-0; this shard declares the
# `@mirror/fracture/keyword` species and treats `@mirror/fracture` as
# the substrate's named-but-not-yet-rooted family. A later one-tick
# substrate-pull will declare `prism @mirror/fracture` as the family
# root; this shard stays additive against that landing.
#
# Substrate-pull alternative considered: `@mirror/spectral/oscillate/
# fracture/keyword` (nesting under the kintsugi loop). Rejected:
# fracture bodies are consumed by oscillate's `active_pass`, but they
# live at the morphism altitude (each fracture body emits a morphism
# the loop applies). The substrate-altitude arrow points from
# oscillate INTO fracture bodies; nesting fracture bodies UNDER
# oscillate would invert the arrow. The materialize forward-promise
# already named `@mirror/fracture` as the substrate-pull-correct
# family — this shard honours that naming.
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Input: `opacity` (from `@glass`) — one located fact surfaced by
# `keyword_matches_depth`'s `failure(opacity_map)` verdict. Each
# opacity names ONE offending declaration site: a `prism @X/Y`
# declaration at depth >= 1 whose keyword disagrees with its depth.
#
# Output: `morphism` (from `@mirror/spectral/consent`) — the typed
# candidate the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads from this body
# and proposes through `query_phi`. The morphism's `content` ref
# names the rewritten shard (same path, `prism` replaced by `glass`);
# its `score` carries the dissonance reading (a keyword/depth
# violation is a fixed, low-curvature dissonance — the rewrite is
# unambiguous); its `expected` carries the cadence_kind the loop
# anticipates (authentic — the substrate settles cleanly once the
# keyword tracks the depth).
#
# Spectrally: this fracture body IS one step along the Ricci flow at
# the keyword/depth altitude. The substrate's curvature at a
# `prism @X/Y` site is the keyword/depth mismatch; the negative-
# curvature direction IS the keyword swap; the resolved site has
# zero curvature at this altitude (the depth fully determines the
# keyword). Per `dissonance.mirror`'s `dissonance_as_holonomy`, the
# morphism's score IS the holonomy decrease the swap produces.
#
# Audibly: this fracture body IS the audible-altitude V → I cadence
# at the keyword/depth altitude. The pre-rewrite state holds the
# dominant tension (the wrong keyword); the post-rewrite state
# resolves to the tonic (the right keyword); the cadence is
# authentic (cadence.mirror's `authentic` variant).
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@glass`, `opacity` is the substrate's located-fact carrier;
# this shard reads it directly. Per `@mirror/spectral/consent`,
# `morphism` is the substrate's typed-candidate carrier; this shard
# emits it directly. Per `@mirror/spectral/morphism`, `morphism_context`
# is the per-candidate slice that pairs a candidate with its
# pre-anchor; this shard's emitted morphism is consumed by the loop
# AND lifted into a morphism_context via `paired(oscillation.anchor,
# m)` at the active_pass altitude. Per
# `@epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth`, the consuming
# property's `keyword_matches_depth(file: ref) -> transparency` is
# the gate that surfaces the opacity this body resolves.
#
# NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-`ref`
# carriers where structured types are available (per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]). The fracture body reads typed opacity,
# emits typed morphism — the substrate's vocabulary throughout.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
#   - `resolve_keyword` reads one opacity at a time. The property's
#     `failure(opacity_map)` carries [opacity]; the kintsugi loop
#     iterates the map and calls `resolve_keyword` per opacity. The
#     substrate names the per-site resolution; the iteration is the
#     loop's concern, not this body's.
#
#   - The morphism's `content: ref` carries the substrate handle to
#     the rewritten shard. The realisation layer produces the
#     rewritten splinter (same path, keyword swapped) and passes its
#     handle as the morphism's content. The substrate names the
#     shape of the proposal; the byte-level rewrite rides the
#     realisation layer's @mirror/store discipline.
#
#   - The `expected: cadence_kind` field is `authentic` for this
#     fracture body — the keyword/depth rule is deterministic and
#     resolution always settles cleanly. The substrate names the
#     cadence anticipation; the kintsugi loop's `read_consent`
#     bridges the verdict to the next oscillation_state.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   fracture          Galen (~170 CE) On Fractures and Joints; the
#                     reduction of a fracture IS the restoration of
#                     anatomical alignment. The substrate's reading
#                     is Bonnemain (1996) on the typed bonesetter's
#                     decision tree: the fracture pattern determines
#                     the reduction technique. This body IS the
#                     reduction for the keyword/depth pattern.
#   keyword swap      Spencer-Brown (1969) Laws of Form §2; the
#                     distinction primitive — calling a different
#                     name re-marks the boundary. The substrate's
#                     keyword distinction (prism vs glass) IS the
#                     boundary; this body re-marks the boundary
#                     when the path-altitude drifts.
#   reduction         Aristotle (~350 BCE) Posterior Analytics; the
#                     resolution of a complex form to a simpler one.
#                     The substrate's reading is Lawvere & Schanuel
#                     (1997) Conceptual Mathematics — categorical
#                     reduction collapses two arrows into one when
#                     the diagram commutes. This body's reduction
#                     collapses the keyword/depth mismatch when the
#                     swap makes the path commute.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the per-site reduction so
# the kintsugi loop reads it. No invention.
#
# Spec context: recognition #46 (the keyword/depth boundary; pending
#               promotion); recognition #51 (mirror as expanding
#               Hilbert space; promoted) — the keyword tracks the
#               Bateson level; this fracture body restores tracking.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (opacity is substrate vocabulary; the fracture
#                      reads the typed carrier rather than threading
#                      an opaque ref through the loop),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (the
#                      kintsugi loop's bias direction is substrate-
#                      pull — keyword/depth alignment IS one
#                      coordinate of the substrate-pull gradient;
#                      this fracture body fits the bias),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (Ashby's
#                      requisite variety — the keyword vocabulary
#                      partitions the @ path-space into
#                      depth-classes; the fracture body maintains
#                      the partition under mutation),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity and
#                      morphism are typed carriers; the body does
#                      NOT escape as a bare (location, keyword)
#                      tuple),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the substrate had `glass` since
#                      shards/glass.mirror:94; this fracture body
#                      reads what was already named).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `@mirror/spectral/oscillate`'s
#                  `active_pass` reads this fracture body when the
#                  candidate morphism_set is composed from
#                  property-surfaced opacities; the binding lands
#                  when the kintsugi loop substrate-pulls. This shard
#                  does NOT pull `@mirror/spectral/oscillate` or
#                  `@mirror/spectral/score`; the substrate-altitude
#                  arrow points inward (this fracture body IS
#                  consumed by the loop; not the other way around).
# Related shards: epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth.mirror
#                 (the declarative half of the bilateral; surfaces
#                 the opacities this body resolves),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; `opacity`,
#                 `location`, `transparency`, `verdict`, and the
#                 `glass` keyword itself),
#                 mirror/spectral/consent.mirror (the morphism
#                 carrier this body emits; `query_phi` is the gate
#                 the emitted morphism flows through),
#                 mirror/spectral/morphism.mirror (the
#                 `morphism_context` carrier; the per-candidate
#                 slice the loop pairs this fracture's morphism
#                 with its pre-anchor),
#                 mirror/spectral/oscillate.mirror (the kintsugi
#                 loop driver; `active_pass` is the action that
#                 reads this body when composing the per-pulse
#                 candidate morphism_set),
#                 code/rust/materialize.mirror (the materialize
#                 training set; the forward-promise of
#                 `@mirror/fracture/predicate` as the sibling
#                 fracture body for topology-derived predicates;
#                 the second instance of the bilateral pattern).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/fracture/keyword.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/fracture/keyword` as a species under the
# (forward-promised) `@mirror/fracture` family.
# Keyword/depth property: this declaration is depth-2; per recognition
# #46 it uses `glass`. The shard applies its own rule by birth.

glass @mirror/fracture/keyword {
  focus keyword
  project keyword
  split keyword
  shift keyword
  settle keyword
}

# === resolve_keyword — the fracture body ===
#
# THE AUTO-FRACTURE per Alex's recognition: given an opacity site at
# a `prism @X/Y` declaration (depth >= 1), emit the morphism that
# rewrites it to `glass @X/Y`. Same path, keyword swap.
#
# Reads an opacity (one element of
# `keyword_matches_depth(file).failure(opacity_map)`'s opacity_map);
# emits a candidate morphism the kintsugi loop proposes through
# `query_phi`. The morphism's three fields:
#
#   content   — substrate ref to the rewritten shard. The realisation
#                layer produces a splinter at the same path with the
#                `prism` token replaced by `glass`; the content ref
#                names that splinter's @mirror/store handle.
#   score     — dissonance reading. Keyword/depth violations are
#                fixed-curvature dissonances; the score reads
#                `dissonance.is_pareto` cleanly (one strict winner
#                over the no-op alternative); the realisation reads
#                the keyword/depth altitude's dissonance carrier.
#   expected  — cadence_kind anticipation. Always `authentic` for
#                this fracture body — the keyword swap fully resolves
#                the opacity at this altitude; the loop's `dark_pass`
#                will confirm identity preservation (the path-namespace
#                stays byte-equal; only the keyword token shifts);
#                the loop's `read_consent` bridges (pass, authentic)
#                to the `settled` oscillation_state for this opacity.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# `opacity.location`, parses the file at that location, swaps the
# `prism` token for `glass`, writes the rewritten splinter to
# @mirror/store, projects the new handle into the morphism's
# `content` ref, computes the dissonance score, emits the morphism
# with `expected = authentic`. The substrate names the carrier; the
# arithmetic lands when the kintsugi loop substrate-pulls.
resolve_keyword(opacity: opacity) -> morphism { \ }

out @mirror/fracture/keyword
out resolve_keyword
